# Pimify Caddy site. Installed by script/deploy/install.sh —
# __DOMAIN_HOST__ is substituted at install time.
#
# Caddy fetches and renews TLS certificates by itself (automatic HTTPS) —
# the only one of the three supported proxies that does. Nothing else to
# configure for TLS. Caddy sets X-Forwarded-For/Proto on its own, which is
# what Django's TRUST_PROXY_HEADERS (SECURE_PROXY_SSL_HEADER) reads;
# without it request.is_secure() is False and secure-cookie login fails.
# WhiteNoise serves /static/ and /media/ from Django, so a plain
# reverse_proxy is the whole config.

__DOMAIN_HOST__ {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8000
}
